{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/49959-clarification-on-the-cult-merit","id":49959,"title":"Clarification on the Cult merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-15T12:09:50-08:00","id":49959,"title":"Clarification on the Cult merit","content":"I've reread the Cult section of the rules a few times, but I still have some questions. Is the overall merit rating (0-10) a reflection of the sub-merits, or used to buy sub-merits, or?<br /> <br /> For instance, if you have a starting character and spend 2 dot in Cult and choose the Tribal type, you'd have Reach 1 and Grasp 1. Additional Reach or Grasp costs 2 merit dots, so for instance, you could have Reach 1 and Grasp 2 in this case. What happens if you lose rating, say to a dramatic failure? If you lost Grasp in this case, would you go down to Reach 1, Grasp 1, Cult 0? If not, it is continually more expensive (at least by the original rules) to rebuild your cult, and you could have 10 pts in Cult and still terrible Reach or Grasp if you kept losing it. What if you lost Reach or Grasp when you are at base 0 (before the bonus from cult type)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2012-the-martini","name":"The Martini","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:48:46-08:00","id":50840,"title":"","content":"It's a collection of sub-Merits. Reach 5 is not a five-dot Merit, it's five two-dot Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"